Description:

Without allowspecialusesubfolder, only a direct child of a user's INBOX
can have special-use, however the attribute is set: SETMETADATA, a JMAP
role, Sieve's :specialuse and autocreate now follow the rule CREATE
already did.  Renaming now keeps every special-use mailbox there, not
just those with an attribute in specialuse_protect.


Documentation:

The RFC 6154 note on the RFC support page;
imapd.conf(5), allowspecialusesubfolder.


Config changes:

allowspecialusesubfolder now covers every way special-use is set.


Upgrade instructions:

Existing special-use mailboxes that aren't direct children of INBOX keep
their attributes, but a non-admin can only rename them to a direct child
of INBOX.  Move them up, or set allowspecialusesubfolder.


GitHub issue:

None
